# Commits that changed nothing but formatting, so `git blame` should look
# through them. A single prettier pass rewrites whole files: without this list
# the reformat commit owns every line it touched, and the attribution of the
# code actually written is buried under it.
#
# The repository formats with `pnpm format:write` and the CI gate `pnpm format`
# refuses anything else, so the list stays short by construction. Selection
# rule: commits typed `style(...)` whose change is a prettier reflow of four or
# more files. Single-file passes and one-line fixes are left out — blame noise
# in one file is not worth an entry, and a long list is a list nobody reads.
#
# Enable it locally, once per clone:
#
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# `scripts/repo-config.test.mjs` fails if an entry here stops resolving on the
# branch, is not a `style(...)` commit, or is no longer documented in
# CONTRIBUTING.md — a history rewrite must not be able to turn this file into a
# no-op that still looks correct.

